From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ElXreno <elxreno@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 17:22:38 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: iwlwifi: allow 11ax and 11be in Belarus

The firmware's regulatory capabilities for MCC "BY" set the 11ax and
11be disabled bits, so every rule of the Belarus regdomain carries
NO-HE and NO-EHT and Intel adapters fall back to VHT. Other vendors'
radios run HE and EHT under the same national rules. Keep the
firmware's channel, power and bandwidth rules for BY and clear only
those two bits.
---
 drivers/net/wireless/intel/iwlwifi/iwl-nvm-parse.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/intel/iwlwifi/iwl-nvm-parse.c b/drivers/net/wireless/intel/iwlwifi/iwl-nvm-parse.c
index 863d5e3..9015b87 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/intel/iwlwifi/iwl-nvm-parse.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/intel/iwlwifi/iwl-nvm-parse.c
@@ -1805,6 +1805,11 @@ iwl_parse_nvm_mcc_info(struct iwl_trans *trans,
 	if (puncturing_status)
 		*puncturing_status = reg_capa.puncturing_status;
 
+	if (fw_mcc == ('B' << 8 | 'Y')) {
+		reg_capa.disable_11ax = false;
+		reg_capa.disable_11be = false;
+	}
+
 	for (ch_idx = 0; ch_idx < num_of_ch; ch_idx++) {
 		enum nl80211_band band =
 			iwl_nl80211_band_from_channel_idx(ch_idx);
